# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows writes CRLF into the blobs, so
# the same commit checks out with different bytes on Linux. Two consequences the
# test suite cares about:
#   - `dead-code.test.mjs` asserts no raw control bytes in source files, and a
#     CRLF pair is indistinguishable from a stray CR without a shared rule.
#   - Tests that split source on "\n" see a trailing "\r" on Windows and not on
#     Linux, so the same test can pass in one place and fail in the other.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the repository and checks out LF
# everywhere. The PNGs are binary and must be left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.js   text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.ico  binary